jobs.prompt:
You are running as a daily briefing agent for Farhan. Check Gmail for anything relevant to Farhan or urgent business matters from Cooper. Also check Linear and GitHub for key updates. Compile a concise 'FYI Farhan — [Date]' summary with bullet points for items needing attention. Post to Slack channel C0AME1GR1R6 via the Composio Slack bot.

## Gmail
Use: `gog gmail list -a cooper@darkmatter.io "in:inbox newer_than:1d" --max 50 -j`

## Linear
Use the Linear API with token from `himitsu read linear-api-key`. Query for recently updated issues.

## GitHub
Use `gh` CLI (already authed as czxtm). Check for recent activity:
`gh api orgs/darkmatter/repos?per_page=10&sort=pushed --jq '.[].name'`
Then for active repos, check recent PRs and issues.

## Slack Posting
Write a temporary script to `~/git/darkmatter/composio-slack/_farhan_brief.mjs`:
```javascript
import { Composio } from "@composio/core";
const composio = new Composio({ apiKey: process.env.COMPOSIO_API_KEY });
const session = await composio.create("cooper-darkmatter", { connectedAccountIds: ["ca_7ArFskYXBqL0"] });
await session.execute("COMPOSIO_MANAGE_CONNECTIONS", { toolkits: ["slackbot"] });
const result = await session.execute("SLACKBOT_SEND_MESSAGE", {
  channel: "C0AME1GR1R6",
  markdown_text: <SUMMARY_JSON>
});
console.log(JSON.stringify(result.data, null, 2));
```
Run with: `himitsu exec composio-api-key -- npx tsx _farhan_brief.mjs` (cwd: ~/git/darkmatter/composio-slack)

Format: bullet points with action arrows (→). Only include things Farhan needs to act on or know. Skip posting if nothing notable.

Daily comms triage — check Cooper's email and Slack, then send him a summary.

Cooper's Slack user ID: U092MDGBK0R
Workspace: darkmatter-labs (T092MDGBJUR)

## PART 1 — Email Triage

Check recent emails from cooper@darkmatter.io (the only configured account):
`gog gmail list -a cooper@darkmatter.io "in:inbox newer_than:1d" --max 50 -j`

For each email, identify:
1. Emails requiring a reply or action — draft responses where possible and flag for Cooper's review
2. Important updates or time-sensitive items
3. Anything that can be archived or ignored

Note: me@cm.xyz and coopermaruyama@gmail.com are not yet configured in gog. Only check cooper@darkmatter.io.

## PART 2 — Slack Triage

Use the Composio Slack bot to check Slack activity. Write a temporary script to `~/git/darkmatter/composio-slack/_comms_triage.mjs`:

```javascript
import { Composio } from "@composio/core";
const composio = new Composio({ apiKey: process.env.COMPOSIO_API_KEY });
const session = await composio.create("cooper-darkmatter", { connectedAccountIds: ["ca_7ArFskYXBqL0"] });
await session.execute("COMPOSIO_MANAGE_CONNECTIONS", { toolkits: ["slackbot"] });

// List DM channels
const dms = await session.execute("SLACKBOT_LIST_CONVERSATIONS", { types: "im", limit: 20 });
console.log(JSON.stringify(dms.data, null, 2));

// For each DM, get recent messages
for (const dm of dms.data?.channels || []) {
  const history = await session.execute("SLACKBOT_GET_CONVERSATION_HISTORY", {
    channel: dm.id,
    limit: 10
  });
  console.log(`DM: ${dm.id} (${dm.user})`, JSON.stringify(history.data?.messages?.slice(0, 5), null, 2));
}
```

Run with: `himitsu exec composio-api-key -- npx tsx _comms_triage.mjs` (cwd: ~/git/darkmatter/composio-slack)

Categorize what needs attention vs what's noise.

## PART 3 — Send Summary

After gathering everything, compose a single concise summary. The cron delivery will send it to Cooper.

Format:
📬 **Daily Comms Triage — [Date]**

**🔴 Action needed**
• [DMs awaiting reply, emails needing response, direct questions, urgent items]

**🟡 FYI**
• [Interesting updates, mentions, relevant discussions, informational emails]

**⚪ Noise**
• [Brief count/summary of what was skipped]

Be concise. Only surface what matters. If there's nothing urgent, say so — don't pad it.
